  "audit_notes": [
    "Repository code currently documents internal synthetic validation and a small number of clinician-adjudicated regression ECGs, but does not itself enumerate the historical public datasets used during earlier measurement-engine development.",
    "Because prior exposure was explicitly confirmed for the listed public databases, this registry fails closed and marks all of them development-contaminated.",
    "CODE-test and SPH are consumed external baselines and must not be used for future threshold selection, individual-record debugging, or claims of independent validation for later engine versions.",
    "MIMIC-IV-ECG v1.0 waveforms and machine measurements are open access; linked cardiologist note content remains outside the open ECG release. Frozen measurement validation must not use machine_measurements.csv before inference completes.",
    "MIMIC-IV-ECG frozen external measurement baseline was consumed on 2026-09-28 using 5,000 patients / 5,000 ECGs. Future tuning, threshold selection, and individual-record debugging on MIMIC-IV-ECG are prohibited.",
    "MIMIC-IV-ECG baseline found excellent HR agreement, reasonable PR/axis agreement, material QT underestimation, and a strong positive QRS-duration bias. These findings are historical external evidence only and must not be used to tune this engine generation.",
    "HEEDB was identified after MIMIC measurement validation as a candidate untouched external diagnostic cohort. It is locked before access; no waveform, physician overread, dictionary, or individual label may be inspected until the prespecified diagnostic protocol is frozen and credentialed access is available.",
    "ZZU pECG was locked as an untouched external pediatric diagnostic cohort before any attribute dictionary, diagnosis dictionary, AHA/CHN code table, or individual labels were opened. Only public publication-level metadata and repository absence were used to establish eligibility.",
    "HEEDB credentialing status corrected to awaiting review based on the user's BDSP credentialing page; no HEEDB data access is currently assumed."
  ],
